# UI outcome and feedback acceptance

For every UI implementation or review, use the
[completed-task acceptance checks](../../feedback/README.md#judge-the-completed-user-task),
including consequential states absent from supplied mockups.

When addressing Suggestion box reports, follow the acceptance and archive
procedure owned by [feedback/README.md](../../feedback/README.md#resolution-and-interactive-acceptance).
Reconcile reports older than 48 hours with prior ledgers and actual evidence;
age, a prior “fixed” label, compilation and test counts never establish closure.
For appearance, feel or user flow, require exact-build native interactive
evidence and user acceptance. After overnight or substantial multi-report UI
work, supply the interactive Pass/Fail/Blocked/Untested document defined there.
For substantial UI batches, use its independent intent/experience reviewer as
a second filter on implementation scope and actual native verification evidence.
Start each new build's cases Untested; preserve earlier results separately.
Keep unmet clauses, blocked verification and deferred work open. A user-reported
recurrence reopens the issue despite prior tests or archival. Preserve originals
and history; archive only when the owner's resolution requirements are met.
